Wave Terminal — a terminal emulator with graphical widgets.

The plugin resolves the official prebuilt, per-platform/per-architecture archive
from the GitHub releases API, verifies its sha256 against the digest published
in the release metadata, and unpacks it into the asdf install directory.

Supported hosts (see `lib/releases.py selftest` for the offline matrix):
  macOS   arm64 / x64      -> Wave.app/Contents/MacOS/Wave
  Linux   arm64 / x64      -> waveterm
  Windows x64 (Git Bash)   -> Wave.exe, shimmed as bin/wave.cmd

  asdf list wave              # available versions
  asdf install wave latest    # install newest stable
  asdf global wave latest     # pin it
  asdf reshim wave            # expose the `wave` CLI

Notes:
  * Wave publishes the same Linux CPU under several spellings (x64/amd64/
    x86_64, arm64/aarch64) and only some carry a .zip. The plugin resolves the
    asset at runtime instead of hardcoding a table.

  * GUI on macOS: asdf does not touch /Applications on its own. Run
    lib/link-macos-app.sh to symlink /Applications/Wave.app at the active
    version; it refuses to overwrite a real app bundle. On Linux and Windows
    the installed binary is the app.

  * Unlike `brew install --cask wave`, which installs one auto-updating copy,
    this keeps every version side by side under
    $ASDF_DATA_DIR/installs/wave/<version>, so you can switch between them.
